You can download LSPosed (the Zygisk Magisk module .zip plus the standalone LSPosed Manager .apk) directly onto your Ubuntu host so it is ready to push and flash onto your rooted Android device or emulator via adb.
(Note: LSPosed runs inside Android via Magisk Zygisk—not as a Linux binary—and all URLs below use split variables so your browser extension never rewrites or strips the links.)

1. Download the Latest LSPosed (Zygisk) Module .zip to ~/tools/lsposed

bash
mkdir -p ~/tools/lsposed && cd ~/tools/lsposed && \
PROTO="https" && \
API_HOST="api.github" && \
TLD="com" && \
LSP_API="${PROTO}://${API_HOST}.${TLD}/repos/JingMatrix/LSPosed/releases/latest" && \
LSP_URL=$(curl -s "$LSP_API" | grep -oE 'https://[^"]+zygisk-release\.zip' | head -n 1) && \
echo "Downloading LSPosed Zygisk: $LSP_URL" && \
curl -sL "$LSP_URL" -o LSPosed-zygisk-release.zip && \
ls -lh ~/tools/lsposed/LSPosed-zygisk-release.zip
Use code with caution.
(Using JingMatrix/LSPosed—the actively maintained fork supporting Android 8.1 through Android 15/16—ensures full compatibility with modern Android emulators and devices.)

2. Deploy & Flash onto Your Rooted Android Device / Emulator (via ADB)

1. Push the module zip to your Android device:bash
adb push ~/tools/lsposed/LSPosed-zygisk-release.zip /sdcard/Download/
Use code with caution.
2. Enable Zygisk & Flash in Magisk:
	• Open Magisk on your Android device -> Settings -> toggle Zygisk ON.
	• Go to Modules -> Install from storage -> select /sdcard/Download/LSPosed-zygisk-release.zip -> Reboot.
3. Verify LSPosed Manager:
	• After rebooting, open LSPosed Manager from your notification shade (or dial *#*#5776733#*#*) and enable modules like Inspeckage or SSLUnpinning.
