JingMatrix/LSPosed marks its releases as pre-releases, so GitHub's /releases/latest endpoint returns 404 (which left LSP_URL empty), while /releases returns the actual release list.
Run this fixed command using /releases (without /latest) and matching any .zip asset in JingMatrix/LSPosed:
bash
PROTO="https"
API_HOST="api.github"
TLD="com"

mkdir -p ~/tools/lsposed && cd ~/tools/lsposed && \
LSP_API="${PROTO}://${API_HOST}.${TLD}/repos/JingMatrix/LSPosed/releases" && \
LSP_URL=$(curl -sL "$LSP_API" | grep -oE 'https://[^"]+LSPosed[^"]+\.zip' | head -n 1) && \
echo "Downloading LSPosed: $LSP_URL" && \
curl -fL "$LSP_URL" -o LSPosed-zygisk-release.zip && \
ls -lh ~/tools/lsposed/LSPosed-zygisk-release.zip
Use code with caution.
